---
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user explicitly requests deleting files or directories, do not use Cursor's built-in Delete tool. Use a bounded PowerShell command instead.

For files, use:

```powershell
Remove-Item -LiteralPath '<exact-path>' -Force
```

For an empty directory, use the same command without `-Recurse`. Use:

```powershell
Remove-Item -LiteralPath '<exact-path>' -Recurse -Force
```

only when recursive directory deletion was explicitly requested.

Always use `-LiteralPath` with an explicit path. Do not introduce wildcards, broaden the requested target, or delete unrelated files. Verify deletion with:

```powershell
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath '<exact-path>') { throw 'Deletion verification failed' }
```
